# LocalBook — Claude Context

## What this project does
Full-stack appointment booking web app for local small businesses.
Owners set up services, hours, and availability via a dashboard.
Customers book through a public shareable link (/book/:businessId).
No backend server — Firebase handles auth, database, and hosting.

## Stack
- Frontend: React 18 + Vite + Tailwind CSS
- Auth: Firebase Authentication (Google Sign-In only)
- Database: Firebase Firestore (realtime NoSQL)
- Hosting: Firebase Hosting

## Key files
- src/App.jsx — routing (/, /dashboard, /book/:businessId)
- src/firebase.js — Firebase init (reads VITE_ env vars)
- src/hooks/useAuth.js — auth state listener
- src/pages/Landing.jsx — public homepage + Google Sign-In CTA
- src/pages/Dashboard.jsx — owner dashboard, 5-tab layout
- src/pages/BookingPage.jsx — 4-step public booking flow
- src/components/BusinessSetup.jsx — business profile form
- src/components/ServicesManager.jsx — CRUD for services
- src/components/HoursManager.jsx — set days/time ranges
- src/components/BlockedDates.jsx — calendar to block dates
- src/components/BookingsCalendar.jsx — view + cancel bookings
- src/utils/slots.js — time slot generation (pure functions)
- firestore.rules — Firestore security rules
- firebase.json — hosting + Firestore config

## Env vars (all required, VITE_ prefix for Vite)
- VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY
- VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN
- VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID
- VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET
- VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID
- VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID

## Firestore data structure
- /businesses/{uid} — profile: name, description, address, logoUrl, hours, ownerId
- /businesses/{uid}/services/{id} — name, duration (min), price (nullable)
- /businesses/{uid}/bookings/{id} — customerName, customerEmail, serviceId,
  serviceName, serviceDuration, servicePrice, date (YYYY-MM-DD), time (HH:MM),
  status (confirmed|cancelled), createdAt
- /businesses/{uid}/blockedDates/{YYYY-MM-DD} — date, blockedAt

## Key design decisions
- businessId in URL = Firebase Auth UID (no separate ID generation needed)
- Hours stored as {monday: {enabled, open, close}, ...} on the business doc
- Slots generated client-side from hours + booked times (no Cloud Functions)
- All dates as YYYY-MM-DD strings, times as HH:MM 24h strings

## Rules when editing
- Keep slot logic in src/utils/slots.js — don't inline it in components
- Public booking page has NO auth — only the booking create operation
- Owner dashboard requires auth — ProtectedRoute in App.jsx handles this
- Never store sensitive data in Firestore that violates security rules
